course: dictionary
lesson: 13690
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is needed. «The lawyer proved his client's innocence, so the court set him free.» Here innocence means not guilty of a crime. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a crime, a feeling, or a person's character?
explain: Innocence can also mean not knowing about bad or unpleasant things, especially as a young child. «The story was sad, because the child lost her innocence when she saw the storm destroy her home.» The clue is saw the storm destroy her home: she learned something hard that she did not know before.
explain: Innocence can mean being simple and trusting, sometimes too trusting. «He believed every word the stranger said, in all innocence.» The clue is believed every word: he did not think anyone might be lying. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Innocence is a noun, a word for a state or quality that someone has.
fact: «Innocence» can mean not being guilty of a crime or wrongdoing.
fact: «Innocence» can mean not knowing about bad or unpleasant things, especially as a young child.
fact: «Innocence» can mean being simple and trusting, sometimes too trusting.
fact: Phrases to know: prove your innocence, loss of innocence, in all innocence.
exercise: «The police found proof of his innocence, so he went home.» What does innocence mean in this sentence? | *Not being guilty of the crime | Feeling cold on a winter night | Having lots of money | Being very tired after a long day
exercise: «She smiled in all innocence, not knowing the surprise party was planned.» What does innocence mean here? | Being very clever at keeping secrets | *Not knowing about the plan, and not meaning any harm | Being rude on purpose | Being cross with her friends
exercise: «The story of the child's innocence was sad, because she lost it when she saw the cruel fight.» Find and copy the word that tells you innocence can be lost. | fight | *innocence | story | sad
test: «Mia was sure of her innocence, and she said so to the judge.» What does innocence mean? | Knowing many secret things | Being very young | Being shy and quiet | *Not guilty of wrongdoing
test: What does «loss of innocence» mean? | Being given a prize for good work | *Stopping knowing only good things, after you first learn about bad or cruel things | Forgetting your homework | Being lost on a long walk
exam: Which sentence uses innocence to mean simple and trusting? | The sun was warm, and the grass smelled sweet | *Tom believed every word the stranger said, in all innocence | The judge checked the evidence to prove the man's innocence
